# GST, ITR & TDS Due Dates 2026–27: Complete Tax Compliance Calendar for Accountants in India

**Last Updated: 23 November 2026**

Tax compliance is one of the most important responsibilities of accountants, tax consultants, Chartered Accountants and finance professionals in India. Businesses must regularly comply with GST returns, income tax return filing, TDS/TCS payments, advance tax instalments and various other statutory requirements.

Missing a statutory due date can result in late fees, interest, penalties, loss of eligible tax credits and unnecessary notices from government departments.

With the introduction of the Income-tax Act, 2025, effective from 1 April 2026, tax professionals also need to understand the transition between the Income-tax Act, 1961 and the new Income-tax Act, 2025.

This comprehensive guide covers the important GST, ITR, TDS and TCS due dates for FY 2026–27, along with pending deadlines for FY 2025–26, monthly and quarterly compliance requirements, applicable penalties and practical accounting checklists.

Whether you are maintaining accounts for a private limited company, partnership firm, proprietorship, LLP or individual taxpayer, this compliance calendar will help you organise your statutory responsibilities.

