## 9. Monthly Accounting and Tax Compliance Checklist

An accountant should maintain a structured monthly compliance routine rather than wait until the last few days of the month.

### Every Month

**GST**

- Prepare monthly sales register.
- Prepare purchase register.
- Reconcile GSTR-2B with purchase register.
- Reconcile GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B.
- Verify RCM transactions.
- Review ITC eligibility.
- Check GST payment and ledger balances.
- File applicable GST returns.

**TDS/TCS**

- Review salary and vendor payments.
- Identify transactions liable for TDS.
- Check TDS rates and thresholds.
- Deduct and deposit TDS.
- Reconcile challans.
- Check TCS applicability.
- Update TDS/TCS ledgers.

**Accounting**

- Complete bank reconciliation.
- Reconcile customer and supplier balances.
- Review outstanding receivables and payables.
- Verify expense classifications.
- Review fixed asset additions.
- Check loan and interest balances.
- Review cash and bank balances.
- Prepare monthly profit and loss statements.

### Every Quarter

- File applicable quarterly GST returns.
- File quarterly TDS statements.
- File quarterly TCS statements.
- Reconcile GST ITC.
- Review advance tax estimates.
- Review tax provisions.
- Verify vendor PAN and compliance information.
- Review statutory liabilities.

### Every Financial Year

- Complete year-end ledger scrutiny.
- Reconcile GST turnover.
- Prepare annual GST reconciliation.
- Verify tax audit applicability.
- Complete income tax computation.
- Review depreciation.
- Reconcile TDS and Form 26AS.
- Review AIS and TIS.
- Prepare financial statements.
- File applicable annual returns.
- Complete tax audit and other applicable audit requirements.

